A||||6||The Prezzzz||Need Help on Ball joints||||1||
Z||000000||The Prezzzz||11-11-2001||11:14 AM||||Redoing Ft suspension ( Power Coating and I need the part # for Moog Ball Joint for upper control arm also any one have luck on getting out lower ball joints?<BR>The Prezzzz||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||11-11-2001||12:51 PM||||It would be a great help if you told us what year Fiero you have. They're different for different years.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-11-2001||12:58 PM||||The bottom ones on 84-87 are pressed and spot welded in (if original). You need to gring off the welds then press out the old and press in the new. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||jelly2m8||11-11-2001||08:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>The bottom ones on 84-87 are pressed and spot welded in (if original). You need to gring off the welds then press out the old and press in the new. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats odd, in 14 yeras on working on Fieros, I have yet to see an original welded lower ball joint. I have seen 2 or 3 that had some weld gobbed on there because the hole was stretched out.<P> What is this, a US thing?....;p<P> Our roads are bad enough that you are lucky to get 3 or 4 years on Front ball joints. Like the saying goes, I wish I had a nickel for every one I have replaced. Still havent seen any factory welded ones.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Banzai||11-12-2001||07:21 AM||||I just swapped out the lowers in my '84, yes they were welded in. One spot in the front and one in the back.  Moog #K5292 Problem Solver upper ball joints.  Used the Autozone "Loan a Tool" program for the ball joint press. Left a $104.94 deposit, brought it back in an hour and got the deposit back.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!<P>"I promise Honey, it'll be done in just one MORE week-------"||||reg||1
Z||000005||BRIAN CORNELIUS||11-12-2001||09:36 PM||||The ball joints on my '87 GT were welded in but not spot welded. They were welded all the way around: 360 degrees! I had to us a bi-metal hole saw to cut out the weld and then use a press to push them out. If this is what you find on yours it is probably the only easy way to get it out. Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||11-12-2001||10:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BRIAN CORNELIUS:<BR><B>The ball joints on my '87 GT were welded in but not spot welded. They were welded all the way around: 360 degrees! I had to us a bi-metal hole saw to cut out the weld and then use a press to push them out. If this is what you find on yours it is probably the only easy way to get it out. Good Luck.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well yours must have been replaced by a paranoid!<BR>I did not tack mine at all!<BR>||||reg||1
